-- A handler's enclosing scope is the top level, never the caller's. `local`
-- is in scope at the emit site but not inside the body, so this is an
-- undefined variable — which is what makes a handler's meaning independent
-- of where it happens to be invoked from.
--
-- Refused before the program starts, in both output modes: `verify_defined`
-- (src/verify.rs) is a pre-run pass, not a runtime error. It has to be, since
-- phase 4 — a runtime error inside a handler body is an `Exception` value
-- now, so as a runtime error this would have left `code run` completing
-- happily while `code build` refused to compile it.
Peek => {
    return Ack { "value": local }
}
{
    let local = 1
    emit Peek to this
}
